  "text": "The Facebook Like button turned social approval into a quick, measurable feedback signal. Because a tap creates visible feedback with almost no effort, users gain reasons to post more often and return to check reactions. Likes are harmless decorations because they are too small to change behavior. Small signals can be powerful when they are public, repeated, and tied to status."
